[{"order":1,"type":"heading","text":"High Availability, Scaling Strategies, and Performance Tuning in Jenkins"},{"order":2,"type":"paragraph","text":"As organizations scale their CI/CD pipelines, Jenkins often becomes a mission-critical bottleneck if not properly architected. This tutorial covers advanced strategies for achieving high availability, horizontal scaling, and optimal performance tuning in Jenkins environments."},{"order":3,"type":"heading","text":"1. Achieving High Availability (HA)"},{"order":4,"type":"paragraph","text":"Standard Jenkins architectures rely on a single master node, which represents a single point of failure. To achieve true High Availability, you must ensure that Jenkins state (build history, configurations, plugins) is persisted across shared storage and that a failover mechanism is in place."},{"order":5,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Shared Network File System (NFS): Mount JENKINS_HOME on a highly available, distributed filesystem (like AWS EFS or Google Cloud Filestore) so standby nodes can access configurations."},{"order":6,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Active-Passive Failover: Utilize Kubernetes StatefulSets and persistent volumes with a replica count of 1. If the master pod crashes, Kubernetes spins up a new pod that attaches to the existing persistent volume."},{"order":7,"type":"code","text":"apiVersion: apps/v1
kind: StatefulSet
metadata:
  name: jenkins
spec:
  serviceName: jenkins
  replicas: 1
  template:
    spec:
      containers:
      - name: jenkins
        image: jenkins/jenkins:lts
        volumeMounts:
        - name: jenkins-home
          mountPath: /var/jenkins_home"},{"order":8,"type":"heading","text":"2. Horizontal Scaling Strategies"},{"order":9,"type":"paragraph","text":"Instead of overloading the Jenkins master with heavy build workloads, offload execution to dynamic worker nodes. This isolates jobs and prevents resource starvation."},{"order":10,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Kubernetes Agent Plugin: Spin up ephemeral build agents inside pods on-demand for every pipeline run, and terminate them immediately after completion."},{"order":11,"type":"bullet_point","text":"SSH/JNLP Agents: Provision static virtual machines in AWS, Azure, or VMware and connect them to the master using inbound (JNLP) or outbound (SSH) protocols."},{"order":12,"type":"code","text":"pipeline {
    agent {
        kubernetes {
            yaml '''
apiVersion: v1
kind: Pod
spec:
  containers:
  - name: maven
    image: maven:3.8.4-openjdk-11
    command: ["cat"]
    tty: true
'''
        }
    }
    stages {
        stage('Build') {
            steps {
                sh 'mvn clean package'
            }
        }
    }
}"},{"order":13,"type":"heading","text":"3. Performance Tuning Jenkins Masters"},{"order":14,"type":"paragraph","text":"When your Jenkins master experiences high CPU and memory usage, you need to adjust JVM garbage collection, limit concurrent builds, and optimize file I/O."},{"order":15,"type":"subheading","text":"JVM Garbage Collection and Memory Tuning"},{"order":16,"type":"paragraph","text":"Pass custom JVM arguments to the Jenkins service to improve garbage collection performance and allocate adequate heap space. The G1GC collector is recommended for large enterprise installations."},{"order":17,"type":"code","text":"JAVA_ARGS="-Xms8g -Xmx8g -XX:+UseG1GC -XX:+ExplicitGCInvokesConcurrent -Djenkins.install.runSetupWizard=false""},{"order":18,"type":"subheading","text":"Optimizing Job History and Log Rotations"},{"order":19,"type":"paragraph","text":"Accumulated build logs consume significant disk I/O. Enforce global build log rotation policies to automatically purge old runs and prevent disk exhaustion."},{"order":20,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Navigate to Manage Jenkins -> System Configuration -> BuildDiscarder."},{"order":21,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Set default days to keep logs to 30 and max number of builds to keep to 50."},{"order":22,"type":"heading","text":"Summary"},{"order":23,"type":"paragraph","text":"By implementing distributed agents via Kubernetes, configuring reliable persistent storage for high availability, and tuning JVM garbage collection parameters, you can ensure your Jenkins infrastructure scales smoothly with organizational demand."}]
